IO-44: save and restore Modified Horton's cumulative infiltration Fmh

Commit 353f8fe2 made modHorton_getInfil() limit infiltration with a new
accumulator, THorton.Fmh, but horton_getState() and horton_setState() still
copy only tp and Fe. A run started from a hot start file therefore begins with
Fmh = 0 and can infiltrate the full Fmax again. Store Fmh in the third of the
six infiltration slots that saveRunoff() writes (always 0 until now), so the
file layout does not change; files written before this fix restore Fmh = 0,
which is the current behaviour.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-44_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/infil.c b/src/legacy/engine/infil.c
index dc6a51e..49dee85 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/infil.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/infil.c
@@ -376,12 +376,14 @@ void horton_getState(THorton *infil, double x[])
 {
     x[0] = infil->tp;
     x[1] = infil->Fe;
+    x[2] = infil->Fmh;
 }
 
 void horton_setState(THorton *infil, double x[])
 {
     infil->tp = x[0];
     infil->Fe = x[1];
+    infil->Fmh = x[2];
 }
 
